Final Working Script:

import re

# Sample extracted text list (simulating the extracted PDF text)
new_list = [
    "A LIFE LESS PLASTIC\nRemoved from Register on 15 February 2023\nReason: Ceased to exist\n29-31 Athol Street, Douglas, Isle of Man, IM1 1LB",
    "A LITTLE PIECE OF HOPE\nTo raise money...\nBallakilley Close, Port Erin, Isle of Man, IM9 6BU",
    "A W CLAGUE (DECEASED)\nRemoved from Register on 25 June 2024\nReason: Ceased to exist\nDepartment of Education, Sport and Culture, The Slieau Whallian, Foxdale Road, St. Johns, Isle of Man, IM4 3AS",
    "ACORN\nFor the purpose of...\n2 Marina Close, Onchan, Isle of Man, IM3 4BN",
    "ADMIRAL FETTERIS FOUNDATION\nFor Young People\nStrooan Mooar, Crossag Road, Ballasalla, Isle of Man, IM9 3EF"
]

# Updated regex pattern
pattern = r"((?:[A-Za-z0-9 ,'-]+\n?)+), Isle of Man, ([A-Z0-9 ]{5,7})"

# Extract addresses
addresses = []
for text in new_list:
    match = re.search(pattern, text)
    if match:
        address = f"{match.group(1)}, Isle of Man, {match.group(2)}"
        addresses.append(address)

# Print extracted addresses
print(addresses)


---

Explanation of the Regex:

(?:[A-Za-z0-9 ,'-]+\n?)+ → Captures multiple lines of address content.

Allows letters, numbers, commas, spaces, hyphens, and apostrophes.

\n? ensures it captures multi-line addresses.


, Isle of Man, ([A-Z0-9 ]{5,7}) → Captures the postal code, which is always at the end.



